flowchart TB
  subgraph CLIENT[Untrusted customer and browser boundary]
    HR[HRMS admin and employee frontend]
    HUB[Separate Interns Hub frontend]
  end
  IDP[External Google identity provider]
  subgraph API[Trusted shared API boundary]
    GATE[Portal, active session, RBAC and tenant/object authorization]
    HRS[HRMS identities, applications and batches]
    PMS[PMS authoritative tasks, submissions and reviews]
    FILES[File authorization and expiring application capabilities]
    AUDIT[Request audit: actor, outcome and request ID]
    JOBS[Server-owned scheduler with separate cron secret]
  end
  subgraph DATA[Restricted persistence boundary]
    DB[(Shared PostgreSQL in deployment)]
    BLOB[(Private file storage)]
  end
  HR -->|Bearer session; restricted HR data| GATE
  HUB -->|Intern-only bearer session| GATE
  IDP -->|RS256 signature, issuer, audience, nonce and access-token hash checks| GATE
  GATE --> HRS
  GATE --> PMS
  GATE --> FILES
  GATE --> AUDIT
  JOBS -->|Bounded, idempotent distribution| PMS
  HRS -->|Restricted identity and approval records| DB
  PMS -->|Confidential work and performance history| DB
  AUDIT -->|No credentials, request bodies or raw query values| DB
  FILES -->|Validated storage path| BLOB
  FILES -->|Audience-bound expiring download capability| HUB
